 security:["Propagate source permissions and recheck user access at retrieval; do not rely on a one-time index-time ACL only.","Treat embeddings, chunks and citations as sensitive derivatives and define deletion SLAs.","Restrict connectors, ingestion identities and knowledge administration separately from end-user query access."],
 optimization:["Index only authoritative content, chunk according to document structure and use metadata filters before semantic retrieval.","Refresh incrementally and prioritize high-change sources; full reindexing is expensive and can create availability gaps.","Measure grounded recall, citation correctness, staleness and unauthorized-result rate."],
 watch:["A knowledge answer is only as current and complete as the connector, refresh and source ownership process.","A citation proves source retrieval, not that the generated claim is logically correct.","Cross-tenant ACL mistakes are higher impact than ordinary relevance errors."],
 cost:["Connector/ingestion, storage, embeddings, retrieval, model calls, monitoring and reindexing drive cost.","Avoid embedding duplicate versions and use change detection for stable content.","Estimate cost per indexed document and per grounded task, including refresh frequency."],
